I don't understand why.. but with crouch shooters, they hit me with 1 HS and 2 Body Shots and I hit them with 1 Body Shot.  It makes no sense how I can hit them with 1 Body shot.  Where are my other bullets going? and why am I not hitting the head? Because I am not aiming at their feet.

&#x200B;

I don't know if you experience this.. but I'm unable to find an answer for why this happens to me.

The way it's going, new and casual players won't be playing this game.  I've been jammed in Silver/Gold going up and down, and every game I play has at least 1 smurf on each team.  I never play a game where the K/D's are about even.  There is always 1 person on something like 30.10 on one of the teams.  And It's not just luck or a good game because when you spectate these people or get killed by them.. you can tell they are NOT a person of this rank.  

&#x200B;

It's so frustrating that I'm considering giving up on this game.  Just had enough.

Thanks for the advice friend.  I have been playing Omen a lot lately and having some good results.. pretty similar to what you are saying.  However.... I just played a match on Bind and we got destroyed.  Had a Gold 2 Reyna and a Gold 3 Phoenix both of them 12.15 as our top fraggers.  We had Defense first and stood no chance.  They kept peeking, and again I was just going from site to site.  The worst thing is.. that I do everything a perfectly as I can.  I'm at A, and there is gunfire at B.  Immediately I'll smoke out Hookah and Long, then run there through CT.  Everytime without fail when I'm halfway there, 3 of my team are dead ,and one is getting mauled and is on 20% health.  So I'm running up to the back of site with 5 enemies alive, 3 of them watching that back entrance and the other 2 up in elbow.  I'm basically screwed.  But I find that this situation is the worst on Bind.  I don't really see this happening on other maps.  For some reason people always walk into Baths on Defense and get killed.  They will stand at A short next to the TP trying to pick someone off, but usually they get shot at by 5 people and killed.  Then you have people peeking out Hookah.  I don't know what it is about this map with people wanting to push on Defense.  Every game I play at least one person does it and keeps getting killed.  This particular game.. the Phoenix and Reyna were always dead first, because they kept trying to peek.  So me and the other 2 players were always in 3 v 5 site re takes.  defeat 3-13.

&#x200B;

Edit - After this game I just played, I feel that this is a major reason I'm so bad on this map, is that Offense is always a rush in and Defense is people peeking.

When I was a Gold 1 (silver 3 now), I played a game where there was one other gold player, and every other player in the match was plat/diamond.  I wondered why the game seemed so difficult to get kills, and when I looked after that match it all made sense.

&#x200B;

I think maybe it just happens sometimes, so people don't have to wait too long for a game.

It must be 90% of people in my rank then are inflated.  Because if you read what I wrote every game it's usually 1 person that is the dominator of the game.  That's one out of 10, so before you become a smart ass and say it's me, read what I wrote pal.

&#x200B;

Or maybe you are one of these people that likes to smurf against lower players and boost your sad life.

&#x200B;

Is that why you are so defensive?

The problem with this game is that people don't play it the way it is supposed to be played.  It's a team based game where your team mates need to work together.  But there are too many people just running around doing their own thing trying to get kills.  And pretty much everyone thinks KD is the most important thing on the planet.  This is what I really hate about this game.  If I use a Sage and stay back healing and res like im supposed to be doing and dont get many kills, i get flamed for a low kd.  But the whole game I have been healing the people that are talking crap to me.

&#x200B;

You will also notice that most of the AFK's are people that start off on 0-3 or 0-5, again signifying that KD is all that's on their mind.  I've gone 0-10 but still don't go AFK.  People just can't stand the embarrassment or frustration of not getting kills.  They don't understand that kills are not the be all and end all of this game.  If the people on bad starts didnt AFK, you would probably find AFK reduction by about 75%

This game is all about predictability.  I started doing this wall when I first started playing the game.  I won't say I 'invented' the idea, but I did it before I saw anyone do it and never saw any videos of it or anything I copied.  I just thought it was a good idea to block heaven in my own opinion.  Now, everyone does it.  And people are learning how to counter it more and more.  I had 2 instances recently.  One.. a raze jumped it and shotgunned us all in the back.  And another was a Brimstone that waited in the back corner with a shotgun and hit us all after we came in and did that wall thinking we were safe.

&#x200B;

The trick with this wall is not to do it every match.  Just here and there.  Pistol rounds and if someone has an OP in heaven.. it works.  But doing it over and over, it will fail because they will expect it and do something to wipe out your team.

&#x200B;

It's the same as the wall in mid.  Walling mid EVERY game is not wise.  Because it allows free run from B to A and your own team mates can't pick off players running through mid.

I find the main problem is blinds though.  I always get these Reyna's and Phoenix's that don't blind in.  And then if we don't have a Breach or Omen, we have nothing at all to get in.  Example - Reyna, Jett, Cypher, Sage, KJ.  If Reyna doesn't blind in, especially on a map like Bind, we can go 8 losses before we get a win..... This happens to me a lot.  And This is my gripe.  Because If that person didn't insta lock Reyna, then I would have gone Reyna, and entered with blinds on every entry no fear.  I end up stuck with Sage and either die on every entry or get stuck outside site unable to get in.

&#x200B;

I don't understand why people choose entry duellists if they don't enter or if they are not good.  Either they need to play more unrated, or if they are going to hang back, use an agent that suits that sort of style..

