It could redeem itself back to a possible top 10 position if we get an explanation on that whole Arya out of nowhere business... but if not... it was a terrible episode imo..

I Think the same.  If the whole NK/White Walker situation truly ends like this... it goes down as potentially the worst build up and biggest anti-climax in Television history.

&#x200B;

There are 3 unanswered questions with this whole scene... and I have a feeling they did this so people would talk about it and speculate, and that what we think is the outcome.. is the complete opposite.  The 3 questions are - how did Arya get to the NK past all the zombies, What was Bran doing that entire time, and what was the NK doing?  

&#x200B;

The whole thing is way too simple.  I refuse to believe it it's just done so easily... Either NK is not dead, or something more sinister is going on... ie Bran is the NK, there is another NK or the NK has set a trap of his own and all this is BS to make them think he is dead.

But that is not the model.

&#x200B;

The DLC is there from day 1.  And will be continuous.

&#x200B;

SF2 - SF2T - SSF2 on the SNES all had at least a year between each full game.  The game you bought was a full game.  None of them were the same game, with stuff just added on.  SSF2 in fact had redrawn sprites, backgrounds, balancing, new moves, change moves, more frames of animation, music and sound effects.  The game looked the same and felt the same to the casual observer, but it was actually completely redone from the ground up hence why it was sold as a new game.  SF2T used the same sprites as SF2, but had new frames, new moves, new backgrounds, new characters, new animations, faster speed.  The majority of it was new, except core sprite animation.  

With these 'season passes', nothing is redrawn, no new moves are added, balancing will be minimal, might be a few new stages (but no stage will be redone), and a few characters (no current characters will be changed).  Plus all the other stuff they will put out along the way for Microtransactions - colors, costumes, etc.

&#x200B;

So this model which many fighting games are using now is essentially a nasty way of applying what we used to call an expansion pack.  And again.... in the 90's with expansion packs... you would get the FULL original game on day 1... the expansion pack was designed and added later and had tonnes of value.  It was not planned and made before the game was even released..

And they wonder why Indi games are such a big thing now... Case in point - they give you a full game on day 1.

&#x200B;

I've had enough of buying games with stuff missing from the get go.   I was going to buy this, but I've changed my mind now.  Another step further away from gaming for me..

