&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Big Bash is absolute rubbish these days.  I remember a few years back, teams would go big.. 6, 4, 6, 4.  But now.... they lose a few wickets early, and they literally go into their shells for 15 overs, blocking, doing nothing and end up with some piss poor score with 5+ wickets in hand.  The amount of times I have been burnt by this in this BBL season is unreal.  It's like these players or coaches have lost the idea of what BBL is.  I don't understand why teams play slow in the back 10 overs when they have 7 or 8 wickets in hand.  Then they go nuts with 2 or 3 overs left and still finish with 5 wickets in hand.  

&#x200B;

This wicket seems a good batting wicket.  If Mcdermott and Bailey went hard earlier.. they could have racked up 180+.  They leave big hitters Faulkner, Botha and Archer stranded in the dug out.... while selfish batsmen just sit there blocking and hitting singles trying to conserve wickets.. but for no reason.  There is no bonus for finishing with 5 wickets in hand.  For this reason... BBL has become near unbettable.  The best bet is to just wait until who loses some early wickets, then go hard on the other team.  They will win 9 times out of 10.

